{"assets":["/editorial-assets/cff8548d1e58b863ef37712cf4e7c00710f69734051b60f499141f13e3dfa7a8.png","/editorial-assets/08db8564bedf608b38b1d7c0389df81f1dbef7e9a5592ee445cac7ed81e2404f.png","/editorial-assets/5558a14d7de69b6c4c4deac4462dbdf18509550a2ff971588d54295e69f1ab74.png","/editorial-assets/6e5bea0e923676a8e6f79bf467993a03257a01858fcc2b7d2c91a43a9c05595c.png","/editorial-assets/1e56ca75d4d98b7b3f1a0b1837261758021fbce83d95bc8275f007eb513d55b3.png","/editorial-assets/5d2e2d8db121f43f469550ae7a4667c026893f8e3af282db5840884f4335bd91.png","/editorial-assets/add005d0dfc1db5660979905a31087f30901342920872f9f830542c0a5b0675b.png","/editorial-assets/ea4161b28013e538c97d6a1b264218da14164a58f34367912bf68cdef8aa4c18.png"],"contestId":"721","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"721A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/721/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"721A - One-dimensional Japanese Crossword"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem we have to compute the lengths of all blocks consisting of consecutive black cells. Let's iterate from the left cell of crossword to the end: let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the number of the cell where we are currently; if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and while "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"', we increase "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" by one. When we come to a white cell or to the end of the crossword, we can compute the length of the block we have just passed (it is equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and we need to store this value), and now move to cell "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (make "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). And if we are in a white cell, all we need to do is increase "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" by one. When "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", it means that we have gone through the whole crossword, and now we print the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Time complexity — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), and memory complexity — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"721B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/721/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"721B - Passwords"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The author suggests a solution with formulas: let's count two variables — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the number of passwords that are shorter than Vanya's Codehorses password) and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"le"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the number of passwords that are not longer than Vanya's Codehorses password). Then it's easy to see that in the best case answer will be equal to "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/cff8548d1e58b863ef37712cf4e7c00710f69734051b60f499141f13e3dfa7a8.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", and in the worst case it will be "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/08db8564bedf608b38b1d7c0389df81f1dbef7e9a5592ee445cac7ed81e2404f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Time complexity of solution — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), memory complexity — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"721C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/721/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"721C - Journey"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Author's solution uses dynamic programming. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the minimum time required to arrive at the vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", if we visit "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices (including vertices 1 and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). We have a DAG (directed acyclic graph), so we can compute it recursively (and memory constraints were a bit strict in this problem, so it's better to use recursion to compute it). Let's store the transposed version of the graph: if we had an edge ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") in the input, we will store ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Then our function "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"calc"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), which will compute the answer for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", will be like that: the base of dynamic programming is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1, 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 0, all other states are equal to «-1». If we call "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"calc"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), then it will work like that: if the state we want to compute is incorrect ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < 0), we return a very large integer number (any number that is greater than 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"9"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", because "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"9"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). If the answer for this state has already been calculated, then we return "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" (it is easy do determine: if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≠  - 1, then it has already been calculated). Else we begin to calculate the state. Firstly, let's put "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"INF"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (a number greater than 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"9"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") into "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then look at all the edges beginning in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and try to update "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" with the value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"calc"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"to"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1) + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"to"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the vertex at the endpoint of current edge, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the weight of this edge). If this value is less than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", then we update "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and store the information that our last update in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" was from the vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"to"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". If we try to go by path which doesn't end in the vertex 1, then we get a value which is greater than 10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"9"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", that's because that the only value we didn't denote as  - 1 is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1, 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". So, now we have our "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"calc"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" function, let's compute the answer. We will iterate on the number of vertices in the path from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to 1 in descending order, and if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"calc"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then we have found the answer, now we iterate on the parent vertices we stored while calculating our "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", until we come to vertex 1 (it's important because some participants sent solutions that continued even past vertex 1!) and print the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Time complexity of this solution — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), and mempry complexity — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nm"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"721D"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/721/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"721D - Maxim and Array"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Main idea: we act greedily, trying to make the best possible answer every action (each time we choose an action with minimum possible product after it)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Detailed explanation:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" While we have zeroes in our array, we have to get rid of them, changing each of them exactly one time. Also we keep the quantity of negative numbers — we need it to make the product negative after changing the last zero. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the number of zeroes in the array. If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then we cannot make the product negative or positive (it will always be equal to 0), so any sequence of operations will lead to a correct answer. However, if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then we are able to come to negative product (if the number of negative elements was even, then we subtract "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from one zero and add it to all other zeroes; if the number of negative elements was odd, then we can just add "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to all zeroes)."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If current product is still positive, then we want to change the sign of exactly one element. Its absolute value has to be minimal: suppose we have two elements "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| < |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|; let's prove that if we change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"'s sign, then our answer is wrong. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the minimum number of operations required to change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"'s sign. If we perform "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" operations with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the absolute value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" won't change, and absolute value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" will become "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|. If, on the other hand, we perform "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" operations with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (this may not be optimal, but now we need to prove that if we change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the result will be worse), then the absolute value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" will become "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|, the absolute value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" won't change. The product becomes negative, so we need to maximize the product of absolute values. And then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| > "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| and |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| > |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|, so if we change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the product of absolute values will be less than if we change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Now, until we have performed "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" operations, we choose a number with minimum absolute value and enlarge it (add "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" if this number if positive, subtract if negative). Let's prove that the answer will be optimal. Suppose that this algorithm chooses "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" on some iteration, but we can't get optimal answer if we change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". This means that we can't change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" after this iteration at all (we can reorder our operations in an arbitrary way, and the answer won't change). Suppose we have to change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" instead, and |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| > |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|. Let's consider the sequence of operations leading to the optimal answer when we choose "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and replace change of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" with change of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and let the product of all remaining numbers (the whole array excluding "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" after all operations) be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". If we change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", the total product will be  - (|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")·(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")·|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|, and if we change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", we get  - |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|·(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1))·|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the number of times we change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Now |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| < |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", so (|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")·(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") - |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|·(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1)) = |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"| > 0, so the absolute value of total product will be greater if we change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". This proves that we won't come to unoptimal answer if we change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Time complexity: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/5558a14d7de69b6c4c4deac4462dbdf18509550a2ff971588d54295e69f1ab74.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" if we use a data structure similar to set or priority_queue to get the number with minimal absolute value. Memory complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","te